  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Cornuside and Taste receptor type 2 member 31 through a series of molecular interactions. Cornuside is implicated in targeting Peptide deformylase, which is in turn targeted by Sugiol and Npc158230. Both Sugiol and Npc158230 are predicted to have a target of Taste receptor type 2 member 31. This indicates a possible pathway where Cornuside influences Peptide deformylase, which is a target of multiple compounds, ultimately leading to the activation or modulation of Taste receptor type 2 member 31. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Cornuside affects Peptide deformylase remains unclear. The evidence supports a functional link between Cornuside and Taste receptor type 2 member 31, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and the role of Peptide deformylase in this process.",
